      en: "Canary Wharf is a world-leading financial and business district located in the London Borough of Tower Hamlets on the Isle of Dogs. It was developed on the site of the former West India Docks, which were once part of the busiest port in the world. Following the closure of the docks in the 1980s, the area underwent one of the most ambitious urban regeneration projects ever attempted. Its centerpiece, One Canada Square, became the tallest building in the United Kingdom upon its completion in 1991. Today, the district serves as a global headquarters for numerous international banks, media outlets, and technology firms. Beyond its iconic skyscrapers, Canary Wharf features extensive underground shopping malls, public art installations, and manicured green spaces like Jubilee Park. The area is highly connected via the Docklands Light Railway (DLR), the Jubilee Line, and the Elizabeth Line, ensuring rapid access to central London and beyond. Canary Wharf stands as a symbol of London's modern economic prowess and has increasingly become a sought-after residential destination.",
