      en: "Aberdeen Harbour, now officially known as the Port of Aberdeen, is one of Scotland's most historic and economically significant ports. With a history spanning over 850 years, it is recognized as the oldest existing business in the United Kingdom. The port serves as the central logistical hub for the North Sea offshore energy industry, handling thousands of vessel movements each year. Recently, the port has been expanded through the massive South Harbour project, enabling it to accommodate larger cruise ships and modern support vessels required for the energy transition. This expansion is critical to establishing Aberdeen as a leading location for offshore wind and green technologies. Beyond the energy sector, the port plays a vital role in regional trade and fishing. Continuous infrastructure modernization ensures the region's competitiveness within the global maritime sector.",
